# pango_native_floorplan_compact.fdc -- P15: one compact 2D block, not bands.
#
# Why this is different from v2/v3 (both of which lost):
#   * v2 pinched the *y* band of five full-width vertical strips.  The strips
#     still spanned x=10..117, so the critical path kept crossing the die and
#     the placer lost freedom without gaining locality -- placement WNS got
#     0.6 ns worse and seed 7 flipped from converging to oscillating.
#   * v3 went back to full-height strips (0..199), i.e. essentially no
#     compaction at all.
# Neither experiment asked the only question that matters: the 24.65 ns path is
# 82.5% ROUTE at 0.74 ns/hop, so what happens if the whole datapath is forced
# into a fraction of the die?
#
# Geometry (legal space is x 0..122, y 0..203 -- p13fpcal probes): the core is
# 17.9 k LUT of a 66.6 k LUT device (27%), i.e. ~6.8 k of the ~25 k tiles.
# 96 x 146 = 14.0 k tiles leaves the block at ~48% local utilisation, which is
# loose enough to route and tight enough to halve the average wire length.
#
# Only `soc.core` is bound: it contains cpu + ifu + icache + dcache + lsu, which
# is the entire critical path.  Everything else (AXI, RAM, peripherals) stays
# free so the AXI fabric can still spread out and keep its own routes short.
define_global_attribute {PAP_REGION} {R_CORE_ALL(10,106,15,161)}
define_attribute {i:soc.core} {PAP_REGION} {R_CORE_ALL}
